{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02148",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.26,
      "end_seconds": 9.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.69,
      "text": "Hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second. So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.73,
      "end_seconds": 17.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.25,
      "text": "Yeah, it's a nosebleed that won't stop. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.71,
      "end_seconds": 22.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.51,
      "end_seconds": 33.6,
      "duration_seconds": 9.09,
      "text": "Bisoprolol. I take it 2.5 milligrams, once a day. Ah, I'm on iron tablets, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.81,
      "end_seconds": 53.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Right, when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.02,
      "end_seconds": 57.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "For two months, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.79,
      "end_seconds": 62.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.81,
      "end_seconds": 66.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "About a eight out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.24,
      "end_seconds": 67.94,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.17,
      "end_seconds": 78.47,
      "duration_seconds": 9.3,
      "text": "Oh, and blood down the back of my throat. That's been about the same, two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.6,
      "end_seconds": 85.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "Have you had a nosebleed that won't stop before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.97,
      "end_seconds": 95.62,
      "duration_seconds": 8.65,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened about six months ago, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.92,
      "end_seconds": 101.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Have you had any easy bruising, head injury or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.63,
      "end_seconds": 105.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.74,
      "end_seconds": 110.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Have you had chest pain, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.04,
      "end_seconds": 117.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "No, no chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.86,
      "end_seconds": 120.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.44,
      "end_seconds": 128.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.51,
      "end_seconds": 132.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.86,
      "end_seconds": 138.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Just keyhole surgery on my gallbladder, two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.61,
      "end_seconds": 149.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.46,
      "end_seconds": 159.57,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "Ah, I've had an irregular heartbeat for five years now. Oh, I have low haemoglobin, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.66,
      "end_seconds": 162.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.9,
      "end_seconds": 176.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.86,
      "end_seconds": 182.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.89,
      "end_seconds": 184.72,
      "duration_seconds": 0.83,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.5,
      "end_seconds": 189.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.54,
      "end_seconds": 192.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.88,
      "end_seconds": 195.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.33,
      "end_seconds": 198.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.8,
      "end_seconds": 203.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.91,
      "end_seconds": 206.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.68,
      "end_seconds": 210.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.54,
      "end_seconds": 217.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.57,
      "end_seconds": 221.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.66,
      "end_seconds": 225.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.74,
      "end_seconds": 241.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.22,
      "end_seconds": 265.59,
      "duration_seconds": 10.37,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.9 degrees, pulse is 68 beats a minute, blood pressure 126 over 73. And respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.61,
      "end_seconds": 269.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.87,
      "end_seconds": 273.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.38,
      "end_seconds": 297.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "There is a bleeding point on the front of the septum and the nose has been dry."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.93,
      "end_seconds": 309.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.78,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Putting it all together, it points towards an anterior nosebleed on a blood thinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.73,
      "end_seconds": 315.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.57,
      "end_seconds": 354.74,
      "duration_seconds": 35.17,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now an anterior nosebleed on a blood thinner is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'm sending you for a blood count because of epistaxis. We should do a clotting test for epistaxis on anticoagulant. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Lean forward and pinch the soft part of the nose for fifteen minutes; I will cauterise the point."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.26,
      "end_seconds": 371.59,
      "duration_seconds": 16.33,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. One warning sign to remember: the bleeding does not stop after twenty minutes. In that case don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.11,
      "end_seconds": 374.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Yes, will do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.02,
      "end_seconds": 381.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "We'll catch up in one week. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.22,
      "end_seconds": 385.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}